meta {
  name: DELETE Settings Business Hours
  type: http
  seq: 78
}

delete {
  url: {{baseURL}}/recommendations/openshift/settings/business-hours
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  x-rh-identity: {{xRhIdentity}}
}

docs {
  With RBAC enabled, DELETE requires wildcard `cost-management:settings:write`.
  A permission-denied 403 must preserve the existing org schedule, business-hours
  digests and pending state, without reship or cache changes. Environment locks
  are an independent denial reason with their existing error/locked response.

  Authorized DELETE is destructive: it removes the org override and can prune
  digests and request historical reship. Run permission/state-preservation checks
  only in an explicitly disposable org with a seeded non-default schedule and
  a real read-only caller. Verify the unchanged schedule afterward, not only 403.
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}
